{
  "name": "cerberus",
  "mount": { "h": 2.4, "speed": 1.8 },
  "_about": "CERBERUS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/monsters/cerberus.py, written whole from the grey wolf: wolf_base.json there): the three-headed hound that guards the underworld's gate -- a black mastiff-built wolf 1.5x a grey wolf's size (withers ~1.1 m), the withers, shoulders and chest broadened and deepened, heavy legs and paws with hooked `horn` claws, one a toe. THREE HEADS on three thick necks from the shoulders: the centre one the rig's own `head` and `neck` (its idle look-around, an.look); the side ones the centre's head-and-neck group turned 32 degrees out and 10 more up about the neck's root and set out 0.26 m (broad shoulder masses under them), on bones of their own (extras: neckL -> headL -> headJawL, mirrored R) -- the right head every left shape's mirror, so the rest mesh is mirror-symmetric (mesh.symmetric). Each head a wolf's: erect cupped `fin` ears, dark whiskers, EMBER eyes (slit pupils, ember-red lids), the MOUTH OPEN in a snarl -- the lower jaw turned 20 degrees down on its own JAW bone, a dark mouth and a tongue between, the muzzle wrinkled, `horn` teeth (canines, incisors, premolars and the carnassial, upper on the head, lower on the jaw, rooted by rays through the lips). EVERY HEAD MOVES on the idle clock, each on its own speed and phase: the heads look about (y), the side necks rise and fall (z: a howl's lift), each jaw snaps wider now and then (a flick). A MANE of dark bristling quills (`coat`) on the necks and the shoulders. The TAIL a SERPENT: one scaled `sweep` along tail..tail5 (raw parts, each swaying a beat behind the last: a wave runs down it), rising at its end into a snake's head (tail5: scaled cranium and snout, amber slit eyes, two small `horn` fangs, a red forked tongue) that looks about. It howls as the wolf does (call). In the monster pen (MFENCE: `monster`; the world has no cave, ruin or underworld gate to set it at).",
